        {
          "headline": "Preprint: bedside-only distilled model predicted 7-day adverse outcomes in upper GI bleeding at AUC 0.848",
          "sources": [
            { "name": "medRxiv", "url": "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.11.24.26368922v1" }
          ],
          "bullets": [
            "Retrospective analysis of 601 acute upper gastrointestinal bleeding patients admitted to the emergency department of the First Medical Center of the Chinese PLA General Hospital between December 2023 and January 2025. A teacher model trained on full-dimensional clinical indicators was distilled into a student model using 11 bedside-obtainable features, excluding haematological indicators.",
            "The best student model, LightGBM, reached AUC 0.848, accuracy 0.826, precision 0.750, recall 0.732, F1 0.741 and a Brier score of 0.128. SHAP ranked Glasgow Coma Scale, age and sex highest.",
            "The abstract states its AUC was higher than the pre-endoscopic Rockall score, Shock Index, Age-Shock Index and Modified Shock Index (P<0.05), and higher but not significantly so than Glasgow-Blatchford and AIMS-65. It is a single-centre retrospective study and is not peer reviewed."
